.TH LOGANALYZER 1 "November 2026" "OS I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
loganalyzer \- count log lines, levels and keyword occurrences with mmap
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loganalyzer
.RB [ -k " keyword" ]
.RB [ -v ]
.I FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Map a regular log file read-only with mmap and count lines containing ERROR, WARN and INFO. These categories can overlap. Keyword matching is case-sensitive and literal. -v prints matching lines when -k is specified; lines are truncated to 1000 bytes for display.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -k " keyword"
Count lines containing keyword.
.TP
.B -v
Print matching lines with line numbers.
.TP
.B -h
Print usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 2 invalid arguments or file errors.
.SH NOTES
Only regular files are accepted. No log format or timestamp parsing is assumed.
